comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-31T15:52:49.264Z","harness:claude-code","Follow-on effect, found by hosted coverage on PR #1638: a completion transaction (close → release) no longer has a release with ownership effects of its own, because closure now clears the claim. The existing post-release-failure test therefore stopped reaching the release step's compensation in `src/sdk/item-transaction.ts`. A dedicated test now covers that path: claim, then a transaction of release followed by a failing step, then assert the assignee and claim principal are restored. The completion plan keeps its release step, which stays a harmless no-op after close.\n"
